# What Prettier does not touch, and why.
#
# The rule: Prettier governs code, not prose and not generated files. It was
# installed, never enforced, and 152 files had drifted from it — so the question
# was not "which files does it already own" but "which files should it own".

# --- Prose ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Every markdown file here is hand-wrapped at about eighty columns and written
# as prose: the decision records, the worklists, STATE.md, the instructions in
# CLAUDE.md. Prettier reflows markdown, which would rewrite the line breaks of
# ~60 documents whose paragraphs were shaped deliberately. Nothing is gained;
# the diffs of every future edit get noisier.
*.md

# --- Generated ----------------------------------------------------------
# Written by a script, checked by a script, never edited by hand. Formatting
# them means the generator and the formatter can disagree, and the generator
# wins every time it runs.
*.generated.json
*.undo.json
# pnpm writes and reads this one; a reflow of it is a merge conflict waiting to happen.
pnpm-lock.yaml
# Rows lifted verbatim out of Postgres so they can be pasted back. Reformatting
# them would be editing a record of what the database held.
docs/*.json

# Supabase's auth email templates are HTML that Supabase renders and its own
# tooling round-trips; public/ holds assets generated in the iOS repo.
supabase/templates/
supabase/.temp/
public/
.next/
node_modules/
.context/

# Claude's worktrees live inside the checkout, each a whole copy of this repo.
# Without this every tool reads the repo two or three times over.
.claude/
